    [Feature] Route strided MLA cache writes through PROLOG_V3 (#18256)
    
    ### What does this PR do?
    
    Replaces the `npu_kv_rmsnorm_rope_cache` writer with `npu_mla_prolog_v3`
    for strided MLA caches on A2/A3/A5.
    
    ### Key changes
    
    - Route component-major and token-fused MLA caches through
    `npu_mla_prolog_v3`
    - Reuse the PROLOG_V3 weight preparation path for DSpark context writes
    - Add CPU routing tests for:
      - A2/A3 component-major cache
      - A5 token-fused cache
      - decode/prefill routing
      - FA-quant query mode
    
    ### Why is this needed?
    
    `aclnnKvRmsNormRopeCache` marks cache inputs as `AutoContiguous`, which
    can materialize a large contiguous copy for strided MLA caches and cause
    OOM during graph warmup. `npu_mla_prolog_v3` marks the cache inputs as
    `IgnoreContiguous` and supports the strided cache layout directly.
    
    ### Notes
    
    - This PR is based on the strided MLA cache work from #16456.
    - The baseline PR keeps the existing `rmsnorm_rope` path; this PR
    switches the writer to PROLOG_V3.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
